    "title": "pandas.Period.year — pandas 3.1.0.dev0+1661.gf74cda2e6e documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.Period.year#\n\n- Period.year#\n- Return the year this Period falls on. The year is derived from the internal representation of the Period based on its ordinal value and frequency. \n  - Returns:\n    - int\n See also \n  - `period.month`\n  - Get the month of the year for the given Period.\n  - `period.day`\n  - Return the day of the month the Period falls on.\n Notes The year is based on the ordinal and base attributes of the Period. Examples Create a Period object for January 2023 and get the year: >>> period = pd.Period('2023-01', 'M') >>> period.year 2023 Create a Period object for 01 January 2023 and get the year: >>> period = pd.Period('2023', 'D') >>> period.year 2023 Get the year for a period representing a quarter: >>> period = pd.Period('2023Q2', 'Q') >>> period.year 2023 Handle a case where the Period object is empty, which results in NaN: >>> period = pd.Period('nan', 'M') >>> period.year nan",
